The open letter included in OPEN_LETTER.md and in the source-code comments is a
statement of the faith and purpose behind Project GILOA. It does not itself
constitute a software license or grant permission to use the software.

Community participation
-----------------------
Project GILOA is intended to welcome collaborative participation in Teachable
Machine training, real-world place marking, and the creation of local data and
content. A person who agrees to the official contribution methods and
guidelines published by the copyright holder in the future may contribute to
the official GILOA platform within the scope of those guidelines.

Permission to contribute does not grant a right to copy the project as a whole
or to distribute, operate, sell, sublicense, or separate it into another
platform. To preserve one shared world connecting real and online experiences,
the permitted use and rights associated with contributions will be governed by
the official contribution guidelines and any separate terms of agreement.
Until those guidelines are published, this paragraph grants no additional
permission.
